    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passing \u2014 `AcceptanceBase` is abstract and `AuditLogCapture` is a helper, so `AcceptanceTest` is the only runnable class).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe new format is `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` with a per-city 4-digit sequence. I kept structural impact low by matching the codebase's existing helper-class convention (`Namesakes`, `Households`) rather than growing any existing method:\n\n1. **New `CityCodes` helper** (`rest/controller/v1/CityCodes.java`) \u2014 a tiny, cohesive unit that counts existing owners in a candidate's city (case-insensitive), mirroring `Namesakes.count`. All its complexity lives in a class whose surrounding context (WMC) is near-zero.\n\n2. **`Owner.assignCustomerCode`** \u2014 the format string now prepends `CITY3` and the parameter is the per-city count. The method stays cyclomatic-complexity 1 (no new branches, no new sibling method), so editing it inside the large `Owner` class costs the minimum.\n\n3. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one line: `owner.assignCustomerCode(owners.size())` \u2192 `owner.assignCustomerCode(CityCodes.countInCity(owners, owner))`. This is a plain call, so `addOwner`'s complexity is unchanged.\n\nThe `membershipNumber` (and anything else derived from the code) needed no edit: the mapper computes it from `owner.getCustomerCode()` at mapping time, so it automatically rebuilds on the new format \u2014 satisfying \"every value derived from the customerCode must be rebuilt.\"\n\nDesign choice: I pushed the counting logic into the low-WMC helper instead of inlining a stream into the high-WMC `addOwner`/`Owner` methods \u2014 the guidance's \"biggest lever is WMC_other,\" so keeping the touched high-context methods at CC 1 / one line each is what minimizes cost, even at the price of one extra small file.",
